<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">S. W. R. D. Bandaranaike</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1899">1899</a>–<a href="/years/1959">1959</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">S. W. R. D. Bandaranaike was Prime Minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceylon">Ceylon</a> from 1956 until his assassination in 1959. He founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a> Freedom Party in 1951 and won the 1956 election on a Sinhalese nationalist programme, passing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sinhala-only-act">Sinhala Only Act</a>, which made Sinhala the sole official language. He was shot by a Buddhist monk, and his widow <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sirimavo-bandaranaike">Sirimavo Bandaranaike</a> became the world's first woman prime minister in 1960.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/s-w-r-d-bandaranaike.jpg" alt="S. W. R. D. Bandaranaike" width="320" height="401" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: This image is a work of an employee of the Government of Ceylon (Sri Lanka) / Scanned Edited &amp;amp; Uploaded By MediaJet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Official_Photographic_Portrait_of_S.W.R.D.Bandaranayaka_(1899-1959).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
